A) for(a 1 1)  with PathCircleSpace1 = P*(a+1)*2   -> k=4
   for(b 1 2)  with PathCircleSpace2 = P*b*2       -> k=3, 5
B) for(a 0 0)  with coefficient P*(a+1)*4          -> k=4
   for(b 0 1)  plus an extra +2P offset in the body -> k=3, 5
3. Derive the VIA4 graph
Abstract every VIA call to a node pair: near side N_k, mirror side M_k.

For Tr=7 you must get:

代码块


7 rings -> 12 unique adjacent-pair edges
7 duplicate edges (x2) + 5 single edges (x1) = 19 calls
To build Tr=5: delete every edge that touches k=0 or k=1.

代码块


deleted: 6 calls  ->  remaining: 19 - 6 = 13 calls, 8 unique edges
Critical rule — inherit, do not reinvent:

Each surviving edge keeps its original multiplicity and its original direction (l1/l2 order), exactly as it appeared in Tr=7.

Do not "symmetrise" an edge into forward + reverse. Do not dedupe. If an edge was called twice in the same direction, call it twice in the same direction.

4. Write the code
Add CDF param Tr (int, default 7) and PCell param (Tr int 7).
In the callback: clamp turns first, then dispatch — out-of-range values must be corrected before case, and the local turns must be updated too, otherwise the wrong parameter set is applied.
case(Tr ...) with branches (7), (5), and (6) -> error("Tr must be odd number!!").
Both branches must define the same set of tail anchors: out0 / out0m / in6 / in6m and their PointList variables.
Shared tail once: Vertical*, Horizontal*, DiffInput*, VIA3/VIA5, P1–P10.
No debug prints, no time/authorization gate, no Tr=3 branch.
