executable lines (debug comments excluded)
VIA calls as (ordered l1/l2 pair, count) multisets — not just as an unordered set, and not just as a total count.
A matching total with a different multiplicity distribution is still a mismatch.

6. Pitfalls that actually cost time
#	Wrong	Right
1	Tr=5 keeps k=0..4, inner end becomes 4P / renamed in4	Tr=5 keeps k=2..6, inner end stays 6P
2	Reuse Tr=7 nth() indices directly	List length shrank → rebuild indices from the k mapping
3	Swap m4pts / m4mpts, or m3pts / m3mpts	k fixes the side, not just the ring number
4	Treat k=2 as a normal middle ring	k=2 becomes the outer end → single-side grad + MY
5	Symmetrise duplicated VIA edges into forward+reverse	Keep the original same-direction repeat count
6	Clamp Tr after case	Clamp before, and update the local variable
7	Rely on call counts alone to prove equivalence	Counts are necessary, not sufficient — diff the pairs
7. One-line summary
Find the ring index k, anchor at k=6, drop the outer rings for lower Tr, remap indices by k (never by position), and inherit each VIA edge's multiplicity and direction verbatim.
